# Copilot Agent Mode — Tool Output Deduplication for Token Reduction

-----

## WHAT YOU ARE BUILDING

My Python agentic codebase injects tool outputs into the LLM context on every turn:

- File reads (source code, config files)
- Shell / tool command outputs
- API call responses
- RAG / document retrieval results

The problem: the SAME content gets re-injected multiple times across turns.
Every re-injection costs the same tokens as the first injection.

You are building a deduplication layer that:

1. Intercepts every piece of content BEFORE it is injected into context
1. On first occurrence: stores the content, injects it normally
1. On repeat occurrence: injects a short reference token instead (e.g. `[ref:a3f9b]`)
1. Tracks tokens saved per turn and per session
1. NEVER removes content the model has not seen yet
1. NEVER modifies or summarizes content — only deduplicates exact repeats

Quality is not impacted because the model already saw the full content
on first injection. Re-sending it adds zero new information.

